From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:48:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Look up key path identifiers by their code units
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Evaluating a key path, checking that a key could be injected, injecting
a key and checking that an injected key is stored looked up each
identifier through the property functions that take a C string.
SpiderMonkey reads that string as Latin-1, so the UTF-8 bytes of a
non-ASCII identifier named another property: with the key path
"my.køi", {my: {køi: 5}} had no key, and the put failed with a
DataError. The QuickJS shim reads UTF-8, so only SpiderMonkey builds
failed.

Each identifier now becomes a property key made from its UTF-16 code
units (JS_AtomizeUCStringN, JS_StringToId), which HasOwnProperty, Get
and CreateDataProperty use by id, in the same steps as before. Array
indices and "length" keep the C-string calls; they are ASCII.

Validation: WPT keypath.any.js "my.køi" passes with SpiderMonkey in its three globals 10 of 10 with `--repeat 10`, and still 10 of 10 with QuickJS; expectations updated with `./mach update-wpt` from both engines' runs. WPT IndexedDB/ (4,511 subtests), 8 processes: host SpiderMonkey 3,288 pass (previous commit: 3,287), with two unexpected sharedworker timeouts, crashtests/create-index and idbindex-rename-abort, that pass 5 of 5 alone; host QuickJS 3,289 (P2.2: 3,289), the one unexpected result the known idbfactory-origin-isolation timeout. /_mozilla/IndexedDB/: all as expected on both engines. The P2 gate at this commit: host SpiderMonkey 3,289, QuickJS 3,290, DAYU200 with QuickJS and RDB 3,286 (P2.2: 3,287, 3,289, 3,285); the unexpected results were known flips: whole-test timeouts of worker and sharedworker variants, each 5 of 5 alone except idbobjectstore-rename-store.any.worker, which times out whenever it shares a browser with an earlier variant, with the P2.1 binary too, and the board's known file_support failure.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent found the Latin-1 lookup, wrote the change, and ran the builds and WPT runs)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
